WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 2: School and Learning.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.880
This unit is all about school and learning.

3
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.520
You will talk about your lessons, your teacher, and
the subjects you study, like mathematics and grammar.

4
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.200
You will learn the words for the supplies you
use every day, such as an eraser and your books.

5
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:23.160
You will find out how to get ready for a contest,
write a short report, and use the library well.

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.040
Best of all, you will learn to talk about things that
happened in the past — what you studied, where you went,

7
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.600
and why you enjoyed it.

8
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.840
By the end, you will be ready to cheer for
the Grammar Champions in this unit’s story!

9
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.560
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:50.560
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name the people,
places, and supplies at school, using words like teacher,

11
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.160
library, and eraser.

12
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:59.340
You will also talk about your school subjects, such
as mathematics and grammar, and say which you prefer.

13
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:07.420
You will also tell about things that happened before,
using the simple past tense (studied, prepared, went).

14
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.100
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:18.780
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
float, throat, coach, toast, notebook, workbook.

16
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:24.080
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

17
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.660
The reading sequence includes A Day at
School and Getting Ready for the Contest.

18
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.240
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

19
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.600
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

20
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.380
The first language focus is The Simple Past Tense.

21
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.660
We use the simple past tense to talk about things that
already happened — yesterday, last week, or a long time ago.

22
00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:53.720
It helps us tell stories and say what we did.

23
00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.020
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.420
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Talk About Your School Day.

25
00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.740
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:14.420
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.660
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:23.100
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:29.520
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
